# UX Copy

The interface is **investor-facing**. Spanish copy must feel premium.

## Principles

- Prefer concise language over full sentences
- Avoid literal / amateur translations
- Use product terminology (see spanish-terminology.mdc)
- Prefer title case for short CTAs and section labels in Spanish when they match product phrases

## Prefer (es)

- Publicar Obra
- Conectar cuenta
- Comprar Licencia
- Liquidación Verificada
- Distribución de Regalías
- Actividad del Protocolo
- Explorador del SDK
- Métricas del Protocolo
- Arquitectura
- Cuenta / Propiedad / Pago / Liquidación / Actividad / Historial

## Avoid (es)

- Subir Canción
- Enviar
- Comprar NFT
- Data / Stuff
- Processing... / Procesando...
- Wallet Address / Transaction Hash / Gas / RPC / Signer / Nonce
- Informal demo chatter in investor surfaces (“Haz clic…”, “stack”, “playground”)
- Beginner blockchain language for end users

## Tone check

If a string sounds like a DIY upload form or a loading spinner from a consumer app, rewrite it for a protocol / capital-markets product.
